.TH DRAGONGL_CLIENT 1 "@DRAGONGL_RELEASE_DATE@" "Dragon GL @DRAGONGL_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dragongl_client \- Dragon GL 3D game client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dragongl_client
[\fIserver_host\fR [\fIport\fR]]
.br
.B dragongl_client
.BR \-h " | " \-\-help " | " \-V " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dragongl_client
is the 3D client of the Dragon GL dungeon crawler. It connects to a
.BR dragongl_server ,
lets the player create or load a character, and renders the dungeon in
real time with a graphical HUD (stats, minimap, equipment, boss trophies,
compass).

Unless
.I server_host
is given on the command line, the client asks for the server host
(default 127.0.0.1), then for the server password and the player
credentials (passwords are read without echo); new players then choose
race, class and alignment.

The map is received from the server in chunks: the client generates no
local world.
.SS Rendering
The client renders with Vulkan 1.3 and dynamic rendering. The scene is
GPU-driven: compute shaders cull the tile and entity instances around the
player and generate their geometry, and a single indirect draw renders
it. It needs a GPU whose driver supports Vulkan 1.3 with a queue family
for graphics, compute and presentation to the window. At start-up the
client lists the GPUs it found and the one it uses (discrete before
integrated before software, then the most device memory).

The window opens at 80% of the screen and can be resized freely; the
swapchain is rebuilt on resize and whenever the driver reports it out of
date. Closing the window or pressing Escape quits.
.SS Disconnection
When the server closes the connection, stops answering (TCP keepalive,
about 90 s) or sends a message the client cannot decode, the client prints
the reason and exits. Server and client must speak the same protocol
version.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I server_host
Host name, IPv4 or IPv6 address of the game server (every address the
name resolves to is tried, 5 s each).
.TP
.I port
TCP port of the game server (default 8080).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_WINDOW
Initial window size as
.IR width x height ,
e.g. 1920x1080.
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_GPU
Use this GPU: its index in the start-up list, or part of its name.
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_VSYNC
Set to 0 to present without waiting for vertical sync (mailbox or
immediate mode, if the driver offers one).
.TP
.B DRAGONGL_SHADER_DIR
Directory of the compiled shaders. By default they are read from
.I shaders/
next to the executable (build tree), then from
.IR @DRAGONGL_PKGDATADIR@/shaders .
.TP
.B VK_INSTANCE_LAYERS
Vulkan layers to enable, colon separated (for example
.BR VK_LAYER_KHRONOS_validation );
names the system does not provide are skipped with a warning.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @DRAGONGL_PKGDATADIR@/shaders/*.spv
Compiled shaders.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dragongl-client (1),
.BR dragongl_server (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Nicola Taibi <nicola.taibi.1967@gmail.com>
.SH LICENSE
